00:02:01.947 --> 00:02:04.496
CHOOSING THE BEST COMPANY

00:02:04.496 --> 00:02:07.699
We must know which are the good companies and on what basis?

00:02:07.724 --> 00:02:10.632
Firstly we will have a look at the incurred claims ratio.

00:02:10.657 --> 00:02:14.697
It means If the company receives Rs 100 from the premium income.

00:02:14.722 --> 00:02:18.656
How much claim will the company distribute from the premium that year?

00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:20.422
If more than Rs 100 claim is distributed...

00:02:20.447 --> 00:02:21.804
that means the company is loss making.

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:25.403
And If it distributes Rs 20-30, it means the company is rejecting a lot of claims...

00:02:25.428 --> 00:02:27.961
or there are a lot of hidden terms and conditions in their policy.

00:02:27.986 --> 00:02:30.820
Using which, it becomes easier for the company to reject the claims.

00:02:30.845 --> 00:02:34.378
So a healthy incurred claims ratio is somewhere around 80%.

00:02:34.378 --> 00:02:39.026
If the company earned a premium of Rs 100, they distributed Rs 80 from the claim...

00:02:39.051 --> 00:02:41.338
and the company will run their business on the remaining Rs 20.

00:02:41.363 --> 00:02:45.111
This is the incurred claims ratio of private &amp; public health insurance companies.

00:02:45.136 --> 00:02:48.280
Individually and average of the last three years.

00:02:48.305 --> 00:02:49.223
If you look at it carefully,

00:02:49.248 --> 00:02:52.150
then National, New India, Oriental, United India...

00:02:52.175 --> 00:02:53.857
which are the public insurance companies.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:56.409
Their incurred claims ratio is quite crazy.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:59.722
That is 140 or 130, all of these are percentages.

00:02:59.747 --> 00:03:04.068
Let's have a look at the next criteria, i.e. the number of complaints per 10,000 claims.

00:03:04.093 --> 00:03:07.272
The average of all the companies is 22 complaints per 10,000 claims.

00:03:07.297 --> 00:03:10.775
We can have a look at those companies, whose complaint data is below 22.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.056
If we look at the lowest,

00:03:12.081 --> 00:03:14.191
then we will get HDFC or ICICI.

00:03:14.216 --> 00:03:17.084
Even Bajaj Allianz, Kotak Mahindra are good names.

00:03:17.084 --> 00:03:18.974
FAMILY FLOATER V/S INDIVIDUAL PLANS

00:03:18.999 --> 00:03:22.741
If you think despite parents, we haven't purchased a policy for ourselves.

00:03:22.766 --> 00:03:25.692
So why not purchase everyone's policy at once.

00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:28.932
Let's take a floater plan, wherein the entire family will be covered.

00:03:28.957 --> 00:03:30.004
You think quite well.

00:03:30.029 --> 00:03:32.523
But firstly you need to understand what a floater plan is...

00:03:32.548 --> 00:03:33.851
Lets say you are four people.

00:03:33.876 --> 00:03:36.360
You and your spouse and your parents.

00:03:36.385 --> 00:03:39.854
You have purchased a floater plan and the total cover is Rs 20 lakhs.

00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:42.593
Now this Rs 20 lakhs is not per person, it's a shared cover.

00:03:42.618 --> 00:03:45.300
If something happens to one family member in a year.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:48.912
And If Rs 10 lakhs get claimed as part of their hospital expense.

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:51.989
Then either for the remaining three members or for all four members.

00:03:52.014 --> 00:03:54.478
In that year, Rs 10 lakhs total will be left.

00:03:54.503 --> 00:03:58.093
Your parents have a higher probability of visiting the hospital than you.

00:03:58.118 --> 00:04:01.167
So they must have a dedicated insurance cover for themselves.

00:04:01.192 --> 00:04:05.433
2. If you club your parents in the same floater plan of yours,

00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:07.959
then despite being fit, health and young.

00:04:07.984 --> 00:04:11.743
You will pay the premium in accordance to a 60 year old person.

00:04:11.768 --> 00:04:12.530
For yourself too.

00:04:12.555 --> 00:04:14.650
Because the eldest member in the group.

00:04:14.675 --> 00:04:18.582
The premium is set based on the senior person's age and pre-existing disease.

00:04:18.607 --> 00:04:22.935
The conclusion is you don't have to involve your parents in one floater policy.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.396
You can take one floater policy for both your parents.

00:04:25.421 --> 00:04:26.891
But you also need to pay attention that,

00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:30.812
If one parent suffers from multiple diseases or is a heart patient, but...

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:32.657
the other parent is fine for now.

00:04:32.682 --> 00:04:35.534
Then you can also separate both of their policies.

00:04:35.559 --> 00:04:37.607
So that your overall premium becomes low.

00:04:37.632 --> 00:04:41.017
And the one's who requires hospitalization the most in the future,

00:04:41.042 --> 00:04:43.626
they must have a good or dedicated cover.

00:04:43.626 --> 00:04:45.768
THE DEADLY TRINITY

00:04:45.793 --> 00:04:49.120
Which features must be included in senior citizens health insurance policy...

00:04:49.145 --> 00:04:52.773
But before that you need to ensure that certain features must definitely not be mentioned.

00:04:52.798 --> 00:04:55.126
And this is what I call the 'Deadly Trinity'.

00:04:55.151 --> 00:04:58.653
Room rent, Co-pay and Disease wise sub limit.

00:04:58.678 --> 00:05:00.657
Firstly I will explain room rent with an example.

00:05:00.682 --> 00:05:03.897
Assume you have a room rent limit of Rs 5000 per day.

00:05:03.922 --> 00:05:05.527
The hospital you happened to visit,

00:05:05.552 --> 00:05:09.578
A room costing Rs 10,000 per day is available, all the others are occupied.

00:05:09.603 --> 00:05:11.937
You get admitted for five days.

00:05:11.962 --> 00:05:14.497
Your treatment costs Rs 4,50,000.

00:05:14.522 --> 00:05:17.610
And your total room rent cost is Rs 50,000.

00:05:17.635 --> 00:05:19.566
But as per Rs 5000 per day,

00:05:19.591 --> 00:05:22.649
you were only allowed Rs 25,000 as total room rent.

00:05:22.674 --> 00:05:27.366
You will think of paying the extra room rent cost of Rs 25,000 by yourself.

00:05:27.391 --> 00:05:30.565
And your claim of Rs 4,75,000 will be passed.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.021
It doesn't happen like that.

00:05:32.046 --> 00:05:35.660
All your treatment expenses are linked with your room rent limit.

00:05:35.685 --> 00:05:37.782
The proportionate deduction is levied on it.

00:05:37.807 --> 00:05:43.365
It means your room rent limit was 50% of your actual room rent cost incurred...

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:46.468
then your entire claim will be passed as 50%, i.e. Rs 2,50,000.

00:05:46.493 --> 00:05:48.224
You have to pay Rs 2,50,000 from your expense.

00:05:48.249 --> 00:05:49.558
The next is co-pay.

00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:53.457
This is straightforward 10, 20 or 30%... anything that you commit.

00:05:53.482 --> 00:05:56.928
You will have to pay a certain percentage of the medical expense from your end.

00:05:56.953 --> 00:05:59.764
Third is the sub limit which is the most dangerous.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:01.767
If you have purchased a Rs 10 lakh policy.

00:06:01.792 --> 00:06:07.565
On the majority diseases or treatments, Rs 3 lakh or Rs 3.5 lakh limit is levied.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:12.058
It means you can't claim Rs 10 lakhs despite paying premium for it.

00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:14.393
And this would be the order to compromise.

00:06:14.418 --> 00:06:17.657
Assume that you don't get the policy without the room rent limit.

00:06:17.682 --> 00:06:20.136
We can take the room rent policy for once.

00:06:20.161 --> 00:06:23.196
How? Because room rent is often linked to your sum insured.

00:06:23.221 --> 00:06:26.976
In most policies, 1% is the room rent limit of the base sum insured.

00:06:27.001 --> 00:06:30.575
It could be less than 1% and oftentimes without writing it in the percentage.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.495
It is defined by room category.

00:06:32.495 --> 00:06:34.021
Single AC Private Room.

00:06:34.046 --> 00:06:35.487
And it's written in the fine print that,

00:06:35.512 --> 00:06:38.489
The most cheapest and private room is allowed.

00:06:38.514 --> 00:06:40.539
If there is 1% of sum insured,

00:06:40.564 --> 00:06:42.417
i.e. on Rs 10 lakhs sum insured...

00:06:42.417 --> 00:06:44.918
you will get a Rs 10,000 room rent limit per day.

00:06:44.943 --> 00:06:46.936
which is fine for most cities.

00:06:46.961 --> 00:06:49.508
And you can take a sum insured worth Rs 15 - 20 lakhs...

00:06:49.533 --> 00:06:52.702
you can modify your rent room upto Rs 15,000 - 20,000.

00:06:52.702 --> 00:06:55.949
The bottom line is... If you increase your sum insured and room rent limit,

00:06:55.974 --> 00:06:57.809
then you will compromise.

00:06:57.834 --> 00:07:00.931
Co-pay, wherein you have to pay 20% of your bill...

00:07:00.956 --> 00:07:03.283
This compromise will be extremely costly.

00:07:03.308 --> 00:07:07.063
And disease wise sub limit will become an illogical policy for you.

00:07:07.088 --> 00:07:09.368
You are also paying a premium of Rs 10 lakhs.

00:07:09.394 --> 00:07:11.091
But you will only be able to claim Rs 3.5 lakhs.

00:07:11.116 --> 00:07:13.625
MUST-HAVE FEATURES

00:07:13.625 --> 00:07:17.672
Now you understand what are the must have features in a senior citizen's policy.

00:07:17.697 --> 00:07:21.007
The first is renewal benefit or no claim bonus.

00:07:21.032 --> 00:07:22.953
No claim bonus by definition states...

00:07:22.953 --> 00:07:27.835
that If you didn't claim for one year, your sum insured will increase the next year.

00:07:27.835 --> 00:07:30.758
It will increase until your base sum insured is doubled.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.498
That means If you have 20% no claim bonus,

00:07:33.523 --> 00:07:35.879
then your sum insured will double in five years.

00:07:35.904 --> 00:07:38.443
Although you must definitely ask your policy bazaar executive that...

00:07:38.443 --> 00:07:40.394
If I claim in the third year...

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:44.204
Will the accumulated no-claim bonus until now...

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:47.390
Now several companies have upgarded no claim bonus,

00:07:47.415 --> 00:07:49.239
and have now started claiming it as renewal benefit.

00:07:49.264 --> 00:07:51.737
Such an upgrade that even If you claim.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:56.340
even then you will get the bonus of 20-50% written as per the condition.

00:07:56.365 --> 00:07:59.569
And in better policies, this isn't removed even after claiming.

00:07:59.594 --> 00:08:03.279
If you get it once, then you can carry forward it lifelong.

00:08:03.304 --> 00:08:06.000
The second feature is kind of an additional cover,

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
For eg: HDFC Ergo, Optima Secure, etc.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.730
You might also get in Aditya Birla's policy.

00:08:10.755 --> 00:08:14.353
The amount of cover you take, you get it's double from day one.

00:08:14.378 --> 00:08:16.388
The third benefit is restoration...

00:08:16.413 --> 00:08:20.442
It means If within a year you have exhausted your base sum insured.

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:24.850
It is restored once, for the same year, for the upcoming claims.

00:08:24.875 --> 00:08:27.304
In certain policies, restoration is allowed one time.

00:08:27.329 --> 00:08:30.274
Whereas, multiple restorations are allowed in certain policies.

00:08:30.299 --> 00:08:32.858
But there are a lot of hidden conditions in it.

00:08:32.883 --> 00:08:34.191
I have explained these conditions in...

00:08:34.216 --> 00:08:38.439
 'The Ultimate Guide to Finding Best Health Insurance Policy' in detail.

00:08:38.464 --> 00:08:40.099
For once remember this thing...

00:08:40.124 --> 00:08:44.119
If you didn't utilize your entire base sum insured in the first claim.

00:08:44.119 --> 00:08:47.737
Let's say your policy is worth Rs 10 lakhs, you claimed Rs 8 lakhs.

00:08:47.762 --> 00:08:49.666
And Rs 2 lakhs are remaining in the base sum insured.

00:08:49.698 --> 00:08:52.034
The next claim you opt for is Rs 6,00,000.

00:08:52.059 --> 00:08:56.253
You will get Rs 2 lakhs, but you will have to pay Rs 4 lakhs from your end.

00:08:56.278 --> 00:09:00.019
Because a condition was written in your policy's restoration benefit.

00:09:00.044 --> 00:09:04.388
That restoration will be applied when your base sum insured will come to zero.

00:09:04.413 --> 00:09:06.344
It has become zero in the second claim.

00:09:06.369 --> 00:09:08.139
You can get that in the third claim.

00:09:08.164 --> 00:09:10.752
But you had to pay Rs 4 lakhs for the second claim from your end.

00:09:10.777 --> 00:09:14.122
But again we are speaking for senior citizens and high risk individuals.

00:09:14.147 --> 00:09:16.846
It could be possible that you might not get this better restoration.

00:09:16.871 --> 00:09:20.056
But still you need to prioritize to take these features...

00:09:20.081 --> 00:09:24.195
because this can increase your base cover to 2x, 3x or even 5x.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:26.910
Less waiting period for pre existing diseases.

00:09:26.935 --> 00:09:28.057
Yes, that's a thing.

00:09:28.082 --> 00:09:29.766
You might have to pay additional for that.

00:09:29.791 --> 00:09:32.736
But depending on the severity of your parents diseases.

00:09:32.761 --> 00:09:35.350
You can pay for that and get some peace of mind.

00:09:35.375 --> 00:09:38.634
2. Less waiting period for special or slow growing diseases.

00:09:38.659 --> 00:09:39.670
which is of two years.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:42.596
You can amend them to two years in certain policies, by paying extra money.

00:09:42.631 --> 00:09:45.108
After that comes, domiciliary hospitalisation...

00:09:45.133 --> 00:09:47.634
which means you can't go to the hospital.

00:09:47.659 --> 00:09:51.262
If you don't have a bed in the hospital, then you get yourself treated at home.

00:09:51.287 --> 00:09:54.590
You can claim the treatment done at home.

00:09:54.615 --> 00:09:57.605
The next feature is pre and post hospitalization expenses.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.343
Before any hospitalization,

00:09:59.368 --> 00:10:04.411
you could spend a lot towards medicine, diagnostics, etc.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:06.795
All those expenses are known as pre-hospitalization.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:09.757
And after a few weeks or months post surgery,

00:10:09.757 --> 00:10:11.919
therapies or medications are continued...

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:14.674
These are called as post hospitalization expenses.

00:10:14.699 --> 00:10:16.240
In good policies,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.551
Pre hospitalization spanning 90 days and...

00:10:18.576 --> 00:10:23.023
post hospitalization expenses spanning 180 days, i.e. 6 months are covered.

00:10:23.048 --> 00:10:28.247
Provided you have proper record of all the expenses with bills, which you will furnish and claim.

00:10:28.272 --> 00:10:31.102
Maybe in the case of senior citizens or pre-existing diseases...

00:10:31.102 --> 00:10:35.206
In this feature, instead of 90 and 180, you might get 60 and 90.

00:10:35.231 --> 00:10:37.129
And some other features such as AYUSH.

00:10:37.154 --> 00:10:45.330
i.e. Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha, and Homoeopathy.

00:10:46.644 --> 00:10:49.224
Yoga and Naturopathy is the same and then Homoeopathy.

00:10:49.224 --> 00:10:50.589
There is a catch in this.

00:10:50.614 --> 00:10:54.527
You can only get claims in the government recognized AYUSH institutions.

00:10:54.552 --> 00:10:58.598
2. You don't get claim in the day care treatment, in most cases.

