He will ensure to remember you entire case and help you at the soonest possible.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.481
Speaking of help in the case of senior citizens.

00:12:37.506 --> 00:12:40.453
A representative of Policy Bazaar will visit your house,

00:12:40.478 --> 00:12:43.938
will help you end to end and get your documentation done.

00:12:43.963 --> 00:12:46.736
So that you spend time with your family members.

00:12:46.736 --> 00:12:48.996
They are doing this in close to 180 cities.

00:12:49.021 --> 00:12:53.079
You can ask whether you have this service in your city while opting for the policy.

00:12:53.104 --> 00:12:55.962
This is very helpful, maybe you are in a different city.

00:12:55.962 --> 00:12:58.383
You can't reach on time to help your parents.

00:12:58.408 --> 00:13:02.433
So a Policy Bazaar team member will get them admitted to the hospital...

00:13:02.433 --> 00:13:04.324
will get all the formalities done.

00:13:04.349 --> 00:13:06.907
3. They have an in house underwriting team.

00:13:06.932 --> 00:13:10.180
What happens oftentimes is when you opt for the policy from a random agent.

00:13:10.205 --> 00:13:14.055
In the process of selling a policy, he might end up issuing a policy.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.658
For which you were not eligible in the first place.

00:13:16.683 --> 00:13:19.545
They might persuade you write a lie in the form...

00:13:19.545 --> 00:13:21.799
and your claim might get rejected because of it.

00:13:21.824 --> 00:13:24.573
He achieved his target, but the loss was yours.

00:13:24.598 --> 00:13:28.000
On the other hand, the in house underwriting team with Policy Bazaar.

00:13:28.025 --> 00:13:29.941
They will analyze your entire profile...

00:13:29.966 --> 00:13:33.237
and recommend only those plans which can be issued for you.

00:13:33.262 --> 00:13:37.681
So once the plan is issued, you won't need to face any issues in the claim process.

00:13:37.706 --> 00:13:39.460
But most people ask whether,

00:13:39.485 --> 00:13:41.500
What If I don't keep anyone as a middleman.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:44.265
I directly purchase the plan from the insurance company from their website.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.959
My only advice is, you should definitely not do this.

00:13:46.984 --> 00:13:50.512
As an individual, you won't be able to fight with the insurance company.

00:13:50.537 --> 00:13:52.380
wherein an aggregator could fight.

00:13:52.405 --> 00:13:56.245
Or else a better agent could fight, who has a huge business with that company.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.843
So If you know an agent personally like this,

00:13:58.868 --> 00:14:00.843
whom you trust, then you can take it from them.

00:14:00.868 --> 00:14:03.344
It's not necessary that you take all the support from one source.

00:14:03.369 --> 00:14:06.665
You are supporting us by watching, liking or sharing the video.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:08.279
But I will tell you something about Policy Bazaar,

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:12.511
They offer several services and will fight with the company on your behalf too.

00:14:12.536 --> 00:14:13.911
Besides, you might be surprised that,

00:14:13.936 --> 00:14:16.151
If you purchase directly from the insurance company,

00:14:16.176 --> 00:14:19.201
then the premium could be similar to what you are getting on Policy Bazaar.

00:14:19.226 --> 00:14:22.862
So it doesn't make any sense, that you leave all these services...

00:14:22.887 --> 00:14:24.256
and you won't get any other service from the company.

00:14:24.256 --> 00:14:27.105
The link to Policy Bazaar is given in the description and top comment.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.044
You click on it.

00:14:28.069 --> 00:14:30.721
And you keep investigating as I go along teaching you...

00:14:30.746 --> 00:14:32.999
Firstly, the Policy Bazaar homepage will appear.

00:14:33.024 --> 00:14:36.828
Once you visit Policy Bazaar's homepage, you must click on Health Insurance.

00:14:36.853 --> 00:14:40.204
Let's say I want to buy a policy for my father and my mother.

00:14:40.229 --> 00:14:43.898
And I considered their age as 62, so they could be qualified as senior citizens.

00:14:43.923 --> 00:14:45.179
Now there is an important step here.

00:14:45.204 --> 00:14:47.283
Here you need to mention your city.

00:14:47.316 --> 00:14:50.022
And this city needs to be where your parents live...

00:14:50.047 --> 00:14:52.538
and where they want to get themselves treated.

00:14:52.563 --> 00:14:54.959
Because, there is a zone based policy in most of the premiums.

00:14:54.984 --> 00:14:58.056
The premium could be cheaper in tier 2 or tier 3 cities.

00:14:58.081 --> 00:15:00.449
Because the medical treatments are also cheaper.

00:15:00.474 --> 00:15:02.601
So If you entered your hometown's address.

00:15:02.626 --> 00:15:06.381
But your parents live in the city and you claim it in the city.

00:15:06.406 --> 00:15:11.265
then either on your policy or claim, 20% - 30% co-pay could be levied.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.011
So don't make this mistake again.

00:15:13.036 --> 00:15:15.116
There are zone based premiums in most policies,

00:15:15.116 --> 00:15:17.056
but there is no punishment of co-pay.

00:15:17.081 --> 00:15:20.635
But they only demand one thing, that your address must be accurate.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:24.219
And most people's claims get rejected because of an inaccurate address.

00:15:24.244 --> 00:15:28.629
If you change the house, then you must update your policy immediately.

00:15:28.654 --> 00:15:31.336
So that you pay the premium for the correct zone.

00:15:31.361 --> 00:15:33.254
You must mention your medical history in the next step.

00:15:33.279 --> 00:15:35.988
Needless to say, If you lie even once.

00:15:36.013 --> 00:15:40.470
Then you might face challenges in claiming your parent's policy worth lakhs.

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:44.448
Hence you must mention the entire medical history of your parents.

00:15:44.473 --> 00:15:47.189
If you think that you don't mention anyone of the diseases, then it would be ok.

00:15:47.214 --> 00:15:48.151
It's definitely not like that.

00:15:48.176 --> 00:15:51.098
Because, you also need to submit your doctor's prescription pads.

00:15:51.123 --> 00:15:54.545
The content written will prove that you suffered from the disease since beginning.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:57.082
For now, I am selecting diabetes and high blood pressure,

00:15:57.107 --> 00:15:58.454
you select as per your illness.

00:15:58.479 --> 00:16:03.345
After that, on the screen, you will be able to view plans of all those companies...

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:07.773
as per the current medical conditions, your parents will get as per their age.

00:16:07.798 --> 00:16:11.379
Now at the beginning of the video, I had mentioned how to filter good companies.

00:16:11.404 --> 00:16:14.318
As per the incurred claims ratio and complaints data,

00:16:14.343 --> 00:16:19.323
I will only talk about HDFC, ICICI and Aditya Birla.

00:16:19.348 --> 00:16:21.626
But I wouldn't bother studying Star Health,

00:16:21.651 --> 00:16:24.000
Niva Bupa, or Care, etc.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.083
Nothing against them, but currently their complaints data is not that good.

00:16:27.108 --> 00:16:29.319
In fact, Star Health is suffering through a lot.

00:16:29.344 --> 00:16:32.218
Because a lot of hospitals and doctors are not happy with Star Health.

00:16:32.243 --> 00:16:35.086
In fact, there is a Doctor's body in Ahmedabad,

00:16:35.111 --> 00:16:37.563
they had banned Star Health.

00:16:37.588 --> 00:16:40.423
If you are in Ahmedabad and you have a Star Health policy,

00:16:40.448 --> 00:16:42.758
then your cashless claim won't be approved.

00:16:42.783 --> 00:16:46.485
Anyway let's move onto HDFC, Aditya Birla and ICICI for now.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:49.614
Firstly, I will select the desired cover.

00:16:49.639 --> 00:16:51.776
Let's say my range is Rs 10 - 24 lakhs.

00:16:51.801 --> 00:16:55.263
Now we can quickly compare these three policies.

00:16:55.288 --> 00:16:57.084
The first point is room rent limit.

00:16:57.109 --> 00:17:00.977
And you might be surprised to know that HDFC and ICICI have room rent limit.

00:17:01.002 --> 00:17:03.186
And you might wonder that the decision is already done...

00:17:03.211 --> 00:17:06.558
Maybe we want to opt for Adity Birla policy, but it's not as simple.

00:17:06.957 --> 00:17:09.196
The room rent limit is in default policy.

00:17:09.221 --> 00:17:11.725
But you can get in and add a rider.

00:17:11.725 --> 00:17:13.780
With that, you can remove your room rent limit.

00:17:13.805 --> 00:17:17.371
After that as I mentioned your focus must be on the base sum insured.

00:17:17.371 --> 00:17:19.937
You get the renewal bonus and restoration benefit as well.

00:17:19.962 --> 00:17:21.932
Because with these two benefits,

00:17:21.957 --> 00:17:25.815
your base sum insured could be double triple or maybe 5x higher.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:29.281
And good to know that there is a renewal bonus on Rs 1.5 lakhs in HDFC.

00:17:29.307 --> 00:17:30.590
This is not a no claim bonus.

00:17:30.615 --> 00:17:33.639
Even If you claim, then every year Rs 1.5 lakhs,

00:17:33.664 --> 00:17:37.404
i.e. you will get 25% of your base sum insured as your bonus.

00:17:37.429 --> 00:17:40.144
It means you will have double cover in the fifth year.

00:17:40.169 --> 00:17:41.884
There is no renewal bonus in Aditya Birla.

00:17:41.909 --> 00:17:44.179
But you can purchase a rider by paying extra.

00:17:44.179 --> 00:17:46.080
And ICICI doesn't have renewal bonus,

00:17:46.105 --> 00:17:49.352
whereas no claim bonus is of Rs 2 lakhs, i.e. 20%.

00:17:49.377 --> 00:17:51.757
The good thing is If you claim someday,

00:17:51.757 --> 00:17:53.757
then your no claim bonus won't reduce.

00:17:53.757 --> 00:17:58.155
So If you cross 5 claim free year, then your cover will be doubled here.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:02.284
And also good to know that in all the three plans, you will get restoration benefit.

00:18:02.309 --> 00:18:04.487
If your base sum insured ends,

00:18:04.512 --> 00:18:07.362
then it will be restored for the next claim in the same year.

00:18:07.387 --> 00:18:10.255
Considering, the condition is not levied on restoration...

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.209
Until now, all three policies look similar.

00:18:13.234 --> 00:18:13.750
Or is it?

00:18:13.775 --> 00:18:15.625
If you look at Aditya Birla's policy,

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.715
then along with Rs 10 lakhs base sum insured...

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.773
Rs 10 lakhs extra from day one is written.

00:18:19.798 --> 00:18:22.911
This is very similar to HDFC Ergo Optima Secure policy.

00:18:22.936 --> 00:18:24.167
This is not a restoration.

00:18:24.192 --> 00:18:27.963
It means from the first day, you can claim Rs 20 lakhs instead Rs 10 lakhs.

00:18:27.988 --> 00:18:30.147
Aditya Birla looks better as per this.

00:18:30.172 --> 00:18:31.794
You can compare more points.

00:18:31.794 --> 00:18:32.936
Such as cashless hospitals.

00:18:32.961 --> 00:18:35.343
You can check good hospitals from your city...

00:18:35.368 --> 00:18:36.972
whether they are in your network or not.

00:18:36.997 --> 00:18:39.466
Also good to know, that in all these three policies.

00:18:39.491 --> 00:18:40.603
There is no co-pay.

00:18:40.628 --> 00:18:43.875
Hospitalization at home, i.e. there is domiciliary hospitalisation.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:45.125
There are ambulance charges.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.530
The waiting period in all three policies are similar.

00:18:47.555 --> 00:18:50.868
But we can reduce this by adding additional rider money.

00:18:50.893 --> 00:18:51.807
You need to do it then.

00:18:51.832 --> 00:18:54.317
When your parents suffer from such a disease, and we think that..

00:18:54.342 --> 00:18:57.231
we can't wait for three more years, we need to claim now.

00:18:57.256 --> 00:18:59.076
You only need to this in Step 1.

00:18:59.101 --> 00:19:01.482
You must compare all three plans in high level.

00:19:01.507 --> 00:19:04.460
By now, you will receive a call from the Policy Bazaar's executive.

00:19:04.485 --> 00:19:08.369
You must tell them your profile, age, pre-existing diseases, etc.

00:19:08.394 --> 00:19:11.632
In fact, let's say 5-10 years, you suffered from cancer...

00:19:11.657 --> 00:19:14.129
brain tumor, brain hemorrhage... whatever.

00:19:14.154 --> 00:19:15.480
If you mention that to the company.

00:19:15.505 --> 00:19:20.057
The company would state that, 'Sir/ Ma'am, we will get a plan issued for you'.

00:19:20.082 --> 00:19:24.526
We will consider this disease as 'Permanent exclusion' and issue the plan.

00:19:24.551 --> 00:19:27.639
You won't get cover on these particular cancer related treatments.

00:19:27.664 --> 00:19:30.049
Or else it could be decided on the severity of the disease.

00:19:30.074 --> 00:19:35.243
Let's say you have diabetes, and your HbA1c is quite high, 10 - 15%.

00:19:35.268 --> 00:19:38.397
So by looking at that, diabetes could be excluded.

00:19:38.422 --> 00:19:41.733
Loading could be levied on your premium or more money could be asked.

00:19:41.758 --> 00:19:42.966
The company could also state that,

00:19:42.991 --> 00:19:45.699
 you will only get a maximum of Rs 10 lakhs sum insured.

00:19:45.724 --> 00:19:47.247
You can't purchase more than that.

00:19:47.272 --> 00:19:49.267
And the premium would be so high that...

00:19:49.292 --> 00:19:51.006
It would seem you've taken a Rs 20-30 lakhs policy.

00:19:51.031 --> 00:19:52.992
So If you have such a disease history.

00:19:53.017 --> 00:19:56.178
So it makes absolute sense that before doing any further research,

00:19:56.203 --> 00:19:58.754
you explain your entire profile to the Policy Bazaar executive.

00:19:58.779 --> 00:20:01.973
And let them come back to you with plans that you can get.

00:20:01.998 --> 00:20:04.540
And those plans could be different from these three plans.

00:20:04.565 --> 00:20:07.169
For example, Aditya Birla has seven more plans.

00:20:07.194 --> 00:20:11.078
They can very well say to you, that instead of giving the 'Active 1' plan.

00:20:11.103 --> 00:20:13.412
They could give 'Active Care Standard Plan'.

00:20:13.437 --> 00:20:15.660
So you will further research about this plan.

00:20:15.685 --> 00:20:17.494
I will keep the cover as Rs 10 lakhs.

00:20:17.494 --> 00:20:19.324
Firstly, we will go to the 'View all features'.

00:20:19.349 --> 00:20:21.405
You will find there is a room rent limit here.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:24.271
Hence you will have to see whether there is an option to remove the rider or not.

00:20:24.296 --> 00:20:26.980
You will get the restoration of Rs 5 lakhs, once a year.

00:20:27.005 --> 00:20:29.594
For unrelated illness. It means it's quite limiting.

00:20:29.619 --> 00:20:32.264
Firstly, on Rs 10 lakhs policy, there is only Rs 5 lakhs restoration.

00:20:32.264 --> 00:20:33.576
There is no 100% restoration.

00:20:33.601 --> 00:20:36.816
Secondly, If you are getting hospitalized for the second time.

00:20:36.841 --> 00:20:39.391
If you are admitted for the same illness, then you won't get the claim.

00:20:39.416 --> 00:20:41.338
i.e. you won't get the restoration benefit.

00:20:41.363 --> 00:20:43.989
After that, instead of renewal bonus, there is no claim bonus.

00:20:44.014 --> 00:20:47.351
It's written as renewal, but in fact it's no claim bonus.

00:20:47.376 --> 00:20:50.331
And you will only receive from Rs 1 - 5 lakhs...

00:20:50.356 --> 00:20:53.770
It means you will get this upto 50% of your sum insured.

00:20:53.795 --> 00:20:56.541
You will get a co-pay of 20% on this.

00:20:56.566 --> 00:20:59.626
You must take this policy, when you don't get anything else...

00:20:59.651 --> 00:21:01.244
and this is your only option.

00:21:01.269 --> 00:21:03.848
Furthermore, you also need to confirm on call.

00:21:03.848 --> 00:21:05.592
Whether there is any sub-limit on this.

00:21:05.617 --> 00:21:07.014
This was the worst-case scenario.

00:21:07.039 --> 00:21:09.855
When company limits tha plan looking at your diseases.

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:12.333
Now let's look at the normal scenario, in case this doesn't happen.

00:21:12.333 --> 00:21:15.252
How to customize the three plans we discussed.

00:21:15.277 --> 00:21:17.158
So first let's look at Aditya Birla 1.

00:21:17.183 --> 00:21:18.642
Sorry Active 1. Have a look.

00:21:18.667 --> 00:21:21.904
The first rider is 'reduction in pre-existing disease waiting period'.

00:21:21.929 --> 00:21:24.793
You can reduce this to 1 or 2 years from 3.

00:21:24.818 --> 00:21:28.288
Accordingly, you will have to pay an additional premium of Rs 10,000.

00:21:28.313 --> 00:21:29.696
The next is super credit.

00:21:29.696 --> 00:21:31.182
This is it's renewal bonus.

00:21:31.207 --> 00:21:34.321
You will get 100% of your base sum insured, every year.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:38.211
Upto 500%, i.e. by the 5th year your policy will increase 5 times.

00:21:38.236 --> 00:21:40.604
If it was Rs 10 lakhs, then it will become Rs 50 lakhs.

00:21:40.629 --> 00:21:44.218
This is a nice feature, which was inbuilt in the previous two policies.

00:21:44.243 --> 00:21:46.396
Although, the bonus was not of 100%.

00:21:46.421 --> 00:21:48.342
It was 25% and 20%.

00:21:48.367 --> 00:21:51.338
Which does give you a decent cover, compared to it's ideal speed.

00:21:51.363 --> 00:21:53.157
But you will have to find pay additionally in this.

00:21:53.182 --> 00:21:54.569
Then consumables cover.

00:21:54.569 --> 00:21:57.051
which is gloves, PPE kit, mask, etc.

00:21:57.076 --> 00:21:59.798
It also becomes a significant part of your medical bill.

00:21:59.823 --> 00:22:02.920
If you need that coverage, you can opt for a separate rider for that.

00:22:02.945 --> 00:22:04.703
And If you have a pre-existing disease,

00:22:04.728 --> 00:22:08.118
which you think you might have to visit the hospital in sometime...

00:22:08.143 --> 00:22:09.881
and you must have it's coverage.

00:22:09.906 --> 00:22:11.717
So there is a chronic care rider.

00:22:11.742 --> 00:22:13.735
Which will give you cover from Day 1.

00:22:13.761 --> 00:22:16.278
Against declared chronic conditions.

00:22:16.303 --> 00:22:18.612
You will tell them cover of which diseases you need...

00:22:18.637 --> 00:22:21.155
and it will be levied once they accept.

00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:25.516
And If the person has BP, diabetes...

00:22:25.541 --> 00:22:27.802
It's consistent and the medications is keeping it stable.

00:22:27.802 --> 00:22:30.709
And If you could push your parents to improve your lifestyle a bit.

00:22:30.734 --> 00:22:34.751
And If you are fairly certain that we won't claim in the next two - three years.

00:22:34.776 --> 00:22:37.132
Then there is no need for you to purchase this rider.

00:22:37.157 --> 00:22:38.153
After that discounts,

00:22:38.178 --> 00:22:40.043
because there is no room rent limit in this.

00:22:40.068 --> 00:22:43.003
But If you want to apply, then we can get a discount on the premium.

00:22:43.028 --> 00:22:45.343
You must not take this.

00:22:45.368 --> 00:22:46.347
You also have an option of Co-pay.

00:22:46.372 --> 00:22:49.661
If you want to opt for co-pay willingly, then you will get a discount on the premium.

00:22:49.686 --> 00:22:50.850
You don't have to take it.

00:22:50.875 --> 00:22:53.271
You have certain similar features in the ICICI plan.

00:22:53.296 --> 00:22:57.611
Just like power booster, which states you will get 100% of sum insured every year.

00:22:57.636 --> 00:22:59.004
There is no limit on this.

00:22:59.029 --> 00:23:00.895
This means If you bought a Rs 10 lakh policy,

00:23:00.895 --> 00:23:02.536
it will become Rs 1 Cr after 10 years.

00:23:02.561 --> 00:23:04.213
It will become Rs 2 Cr, after 20 years later.

00:23:04.238 --> 00:23:05.064
It will keep going on.

00:23:05.089 --> 00:23:09.282
But you need to remember that there is a normal renewal bonus in built of 20%.

00:23:09.307 --> 00:23:12.968
So there is no additional need to purchase it, especially when...

00:23:12.993 --> 00:23:16.795
You won't be able to claim once it reaches Rs 10-20 crore policy.

00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:18.252
Plus this is expensive.

00:23:18.277 --> 00:23:21.087
And it's also written in the conditons, that If you remove the rider later,

00:23:21.112 --> 00:23:24.407
then all the bonus will be removed which you received in this rider.

00:23:24.432 --> 00:23:25.496
So purchase it after thinking carefully.

00:23:25.521 --> 00:23:28.775
There are two types of riders for pre-existing and chronic diseases.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:32.365
Firstly, you can change the waiting period from there to one or two years.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:33.954
You pay the extra premium accordingly.

00:23:33.979 --> 00:23:35.740
And another one is the jumpstart rider.

00:23:35.765 --> 00:23:39.332
In this you will get cover against declared chronic conditions.

00:23:39.357 --> 00:23:41.000
After a waiting period of 30 days.

00:23:41.025 --> 00:23:43.408
These are all the declared conditons mentioned on your screen.

00:23:43.433 --> 00:23:47.487
But there are further conditions, which I had explained in the masterclass video.

00:23:47.512 --> 00:23:50.273
The bottom line is that either the highly paranoid people...

00:23:50.298 --> 00:23:54.963
or people who think they might get hospitalized in a few months.

00:23:54.988 --> 00:23:57.113
It's for them and not for others.

00:23:57.138 --> 00:23:59.381
As I mentioned, there is a room rent limit in this policy.

00:23:59.406 --> 00:24:01.857
To remove that, there is a rider as 'room modifier'...

00:24:01.857 --> 00:24:04.233
you need to select 'any room' and then apply.

00:24:04.258 --> 00:24:07.204
And you need to simply evaluate the HDFC plan.

00:24:07.229 --> 00:24:10.009
If you are getting confused, after evaluating everything,

00:24:10.034 --> 00:24:11.057
then I will summarize it for you.

00:24:11.082 --> 00:24:13.749
Your priority must be high base sum insured.

00:24:13.774 --> 00:24:15.709
Restoration benefit along with that.

00:24:15.709 --> 00:24:17.466
In which, there would be no hidden condition.

00:24:17.491 --> 00:24:19.684
And renewal bonus or no claim bonus.

00:24:19.709 --> 00:24:21.504
So atleast not on day one.

00:24:21.529 --> 00:24:24.876
But after two - three years, you will have double triple coverage.

00:24:24.876 --> 00:24:28.176
After that, you must check the rider of pre-existing disease.

00:24:28.201 --> 00:24:30.000
which reduces the waiting period.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.951
Whether you need to opt for that in your case or not.

00:24:32.976 --> 00:24:34.692
There are several other riders.

00:24:34.717 --> 00:24:37.390
If you keep adding them, then your premium will become unaffordable.

00:24:37.415 --> 00:24:38.814
Hence I am not talking about them.

00:24:38.839 --> 00:24:40.419
And they are applied case by case.

00:24:40.444 --> 00:24:43.326
QUESTIONS TO ASK ON CALL

00:24:43.351 --> 00:24:44.224
Listen carefully now.

00:24:44.249 --> 00:24:47.377
There is a Policy Bazaar link given in the description and top comment.

00:24:47.402 --> 00:24:50.452
Visit the link and do this exercise yourself.

00:24:50.477 --> 00:24:53.582
And once you receive the call of Policy Bazaar executive.

00:24:53.607 --> 00:24:56.610
Listen to the questiions that you must ask them.

00:24:56.635 --> 00:24:59.121
1. Whether room rent limit is included in the policy.

00:24:59.146 --> 00:25:01.947
Listen to what they have to say, for your own sake.

00:25:01.972 --> 00:25:03.868
2. Whether co-pay is included or not.

00:25:03.893 --> 00:25:05.516
Ask them this too. What's the harm anyway.

00:25:05.541 --> 00:25:07.714
This is a must ask question.

00:25:07.739 --> 00:25:11.132
3. Whether disease wise sub limit is included in my policy or not.

00:25:11.157 --> 00:25:14.293
4. How does the restoration benefit work?

00:25:14.318 --> 00:25:17.457
Whether it gets activated on the partial utilisation of the base sum insured.

00:25:17.482 --> 00:25:19.555
or whether it gets activated on full utilisation.

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:20.429
You need to understand this.

00:25:20.454 --> 00:25:25.131
And whether restoration works in both related and unrelated type of illnesses.

00:25:25.156 --> 00:25:27.331
or will you get it on only unrelated illness?

00:25:27.356 --> 00:25:30.564
It means If you get hospitalized for the second time in the same year...

00:25:30.589 --> 00:25:31.787
for the same illness.

00:25:31.812 --> 00:25:34.012
 You won't get restoration in most cases.

00:25:34.037 --> 00:25:35.012
Ask this too.

00:25:35.037 --> 00:25:37.422
If you have domiciliary hospitalisation mentioned in your policy,

00:25:37.447 --> 00:25:39.867
and If you need that as a feature.

00:25:39.892 --> 00:25:41.734
You must ask it's conditions.

00:25:41.759 --> 00:25:43.974
Because every policy has a different condition.

00:25:43.999 --> 00:25:45.202
There is one common condition.

00:25:45.202 --> 00:25:48.580
If doctor has prescribed that you need to be taken home and admitted.

00:25:48.605 --> 00:25:50.613
we will offer cover only then, otherwise we won't.

00:25:50.638 --> 00:25:52.643
But sometimes there is another condition written that...

00:25:52.643 --> 00:25:54.858
because there was no bed available in the hospital.

00:25:54.883 --> 00:25:57.001
You have been brought to the hospital to be admitted.

00:25:57.026 --> 00:25:58.805
We will only give you cover then, otherwise we won't.

00:25:58.830 --> 00:26:00.543
There is a difficult condition.

00:26:00.543 --> 00:26:03.259
SUPER TOP-UP

00:26:03.284 --> 00:26:06.610
Now let's say after considering your parents pre-existing disease.

00:26:06.635 --> 00:26:08.010
Your premium is extremely high.

00:26:08.035 --> 00:26:10.455
You are getting the policy, but loading is very high.

00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:11.857
According to the pre-existing disease.

00:26:11.882 --> 00:26:13.358
So the second way is...

00:26:13.383 --> 00:26:16.844
You reduce your cover, so then your premium is manageable.

00:26:16.869 --> 00:26:18.901
And you take a super top up policy.

00:26:18.926 --> 00:26:21.641
This is not a rider. This is a standalone individual policy.

00:26:21.666 --> 00:26:24.406
There are two kinds of policy -- 1. Top up and 2. Super Top up.

00:26:24.431 --> 00:26:27.076
If I explain in simple terms, then ignore the top up.

00:26:27.101 --> 00:26:28.443
You must take a super top-up.

00:26:28.468 --> 00:26:31.605
The reason is because both policies work in a similar way.

00:26:31.630 --> 00:26:33.599
But both have a deductible limit.

00:26:33.624 --> 00:26:36.085
Let's say that deductible limit in your case is Rs 10 lakhs.

00:26:36.110 --> 00:26:39.612
In both policies, you need to pay Rs 10 lakhs from your end.

00:26:39.612 --> 00:26:41.538
or else you need to claim from your base policy.

00:26:41.563 --> 00:26:45.944
And the amount above that, you can claim from top up or super top up policy...

00:26:45.969 --> 00:26:47.271
The top up policy states that,

00:26:47.296 --> 00:26:51.044
Your bill costing around Rs 10 lakhs must come under one particular bill.

00:26:51.069 --> 00:26:53.473
It will be activated then, which you can claim.

00:26:53.498 --> 00:26:56.214
Assume you have three claims, worth Rs 5 lakhs each.

00:26:56.239 --> 00:26:58.377
Then you will take the first two claims from the base policy.

00:26:58.402 --> 00:27:01.412
And the third claim of Rs 5 lakhs, you won't be able to take that from top up.

00:27:01.437 --> 00:27:03.122
You will have to pay that from your end.

00:27:03.147 --> 00:27:04.941
Because it is less than deductible.

00:27:04.966 --> 00:27:07.665
Whereas the third Rs 5 lakh claim in super top,

00:27:07.690 --> 00:27:09.047
you will be able to do that easily.

00:27:09.072 --> 00:27:11.914
Because you have already paid Rs 10 lakhs by combining the previous two bills.

00:27:11.939 --> 00:27:15.513
And it gets considered as aggregate deductible basis.

00:27:15.538 --> 00:27:16.752
And you will get the claim.

00:27:16.777 --> 00:27:18.674
So long story short, you need to take a Super Top up.

00:27:18.699 --> 00:27:21.066
And the best thing about Super top up policies is that.

00:27:21.091 --> 00:27:24.498
By taking either Rs 40 - 50 lakhs or even Rs 1 Cr super top policy...

00:27:24.523 --> 00:27:28.238
you won't have to pay much as much as the base policy.

00:27:28.263 --> 00:27:30.452
You get such policies for quite a better rate.

00:27:30.477 --> 00:27:32.614
However there are better conditions on it.

00:27:32.639 --> 00:27:33.916
Similar to base policy...

00:27:33.941 --> 00:27:36.371
which you must ask the policy bazaar executive.

00:27:36.396 --> 00:27:40.571
1. Whether there is a room rent limit on super top up policy.

00:27:40.596 --> 00:27:42.638
Yes, there is a room rent limit in this too.

00:27:42.663 --> 00:27:45.512
Please clarify this with your Policy Bazaar executive.

00:27:45.537 --> 00:27:47.244
How much room rent is allowed?

00:27:47.269 --> 00:27:50.936
Visualize this for me in monetary terms, so that I can be at peace.

00:27:50.961 --> 00:27:53.018
But it's best If there are no room rent limits.

00:27:53.043 --> 00:27:55.953
There are super top up policies, wherein there are no room rent limit.

00:27:55.978 --> 00:27:57.813
After that, even in super top policies,

00:27:57.838 --> 00:28:00.234
there are bonus and no claim bonus.

00:28:00.259 --> 00:28:02.698
What is it and how much is it? Ask this.

00:28:02.723 --> 00:28:03.724
The next question you need to ask...

00:28:03.749 --> 00:28:05.987
whether there is co-pay in this. If there is, then how much?

00:28:06.012 --> 00:28:07.520
After that, just like base policy...

00:28:07.520 --> 00:28:10.896
There are pre and post hospitalization expenses in super top up policy too.

00:28:10.921 --> 00:28:13.000
Ask them how many days they are for?

00:28:13.025 --> 00:28:15.957
Lastly, in most super top up policies these days,

00:28:15.982 --> 00:28:17.863
There is a 'waiver of deductible'...

00:28:17.888 --> 00:28:20.551
which means If you gave premium for five years, continuously.

00:28:20.576 --> 00:28:23.404
Your deductible will be waived for now on.

00:28:23.429 --> 00:28:25.428
That means, you won't have to cross Rs 10 lakhs.

00:28:25.453 --> 00:28:29.368
After knowing all this, super top could become a great option for you.

00:28:29.393 --> 00:28:31.983
But one more pro tip which you must always remember...

00:28:32.008 --> 00:28:35.153
Purchase the super top policy the same day you purchase the base policy.

00:28:35.178 --> 00:28:36.972
Ensure the dates don't differ.

00:28:36.997 --> 00:28:38.571
Let's take a basic example.

00:28:38.596 --> 00:28:41.244
Let's say you purchased the base policy on 1st April.

00:28:41.269 --> 00:28:44.431
And you purchased the super top policy next year 1st January.

00:28:44.456 --> 00:28:47.940
So from April to December, you don't have any super top up policy.

00:28:47.965 --> 00:28:49.852
You know you won't be able to claim.

00:28:49.877 --> 00:28:52.951
But let's say two to four years pass, and all the policies are continuously carried out.

00:28:52.976 --> 00:28:55.343
Now presume that you get hospitalized in the month of May.

00:28:55.368 --> 00:28:57.085
And your claim amount comes to Rs 20 lakhs, wherein...

00:28:57.110 --> 00:29:01.572
you claimed Rs 10 lakhs from base policy and Rs 10 lakhs from super top up.

00:29:01.597 --> 00:29:03.818
Because your Rs 10 lakh deductible crossed.

00:29:03.843 --> 00:29:06.965
Now for this entire year in the base policy, you don't have any money left.

00:29:06.965 --> 00:29:10.467
And your super top policy will also get renewed in December.

00:29:10.492 --> 00:29:12.773
So in January, February, March...

00:29:12.798 --> 00:29:17.260
If you receive a claim and you have zero left in your base policy.

00:29:17.285 --> 00:29:20.000
And you have Rs 50 lakhs in super top, just for the name sake.

00:29:20.025 --> 00:29:24.513
But it was recently renewed and you haven't crossed the deductible this year.

00:29:24.513 --> 00:29:27.467
So you will have to pay for the first claim from your end.

00:29:27.492 --> 00:29:29.371
Despite having both the policies.

00:29:29.371 --> 00:29:32.263
So ideally you need to do this planning with the base policy,

00:29:32.263 --> 00:29:33.634
so that you apply it together.

00:29:33.659 --> 00:29:36.208
Even when you purchase the policy on Policy Bazaar,

00:29:36.233 --> 00:29:37.748
wherein you add the riders.

00:29:37.748 --> 00:29:41.610
When you scroll, you will get an option to add the super top up.

00:29:41.635 --> 00:29:44.303
Before adding them, the questions that I mentioned just now.

00:29:44.328 --> 00:29:45.695
You must definitely ask these questions.

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:48.863
As per that, you need to take the company's best super top up policy.

00:29:48.888 --> 00:29:49.920
Pro Tip #2

00:29:49.945 --> 00:29:53.831
If that great super top up policy is mistakenly of the same company...

00:29:53.831 --> 00:29:55.752
whose base policy you are purchasing.

00:29:55.777 --> 00:29:57.660
So it will be a best deal for you.

00:29:57.660 --> 00:29:59.635
Your entire claim could become cashless.

00:29:59.660 --> 00:30:02.014
But unfortunately, the company's base policy you are purchasing.

00:30:02.039 --> 00:30:04.102
Instead of purchasing the super top from the same company...

00:30:04.127 --> 00:30:06.175
if you purchase it from a different company,

00:30:06.175 --> 00:30:09.685
then for super top up, you will have to go for reimbursement in most cases.

00:30:09.710 --> 00:30:10.932
There won't be any cashless claim.

00:30:10.957 --> 00:30:14.334
You do this when you have the super top up policy is better from another company.

00:30:14.359 --> 00:30:16.876
CONCLUSION

00:30:16.876 --> 00:30:20.240
The good features such as renewal benefit, no claim bonus,

00:30:20.265 --> 00:30:22.003
additional cover, restoration, etc.

00:30:22.028 --> 00:30:25.633
If these features are being offered in your profile,

00:30:25.658 --> 00:30:28.264
then you need to apply on those policies.

00:30:28.289 --> 00:30:31.523
You must ask several questions to your Policy Bazaar executive.

00:30:31.548 --> 00:30:34.103
because it's your right to ask questions until you are satisfied.

00:30:34.128 --> 00:30:36.498
Plus, it doesn't cost any money, they will tell you for free.

00:30:36.523 --> 00:30:37.625
I hope this helps.

00:30:37.650 --> 00:30:39.854
Link is in the description. Do check it out.

00:30:39.879 --> 00:30:41.879
Thank you so much.

